---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Commercial Real Estate in Collin County | Ling Jordan, TACS"
  description="Texas Accredited Commercial Specialist serving investors, business owners, and landlords in Frisco, Plano, McKinney, Prosper, and Allen. Retail, office, flex, industrial, multifamily, and land."
  path="/commercial"
>
  <section class="wrap section narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Commercial</p>
    <h1>Commercial real estate, with the credential to back it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I hold the Texas Accredited Commercial Specialist designation. Most agents
      who take a commercial listing do not, and the difference shows up in how
      the deal is underwritten rather than how it is marketed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap section">
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div>
          <h2 style="margin-top:0">What TACS means for you</h2>
          <p>
            The designation requires coursework in commercial contracts, leasing,
            valuation, and investment analysis, and it is administered through
            Texas REALTORS&reg;. In practice it means I read a rent roll, an
            operating statement, and a lease abstract as a matter of routine.
          </p>
          <p>
            Commercial transactions turn on terms buried in the lease and the
            expense structure &mdash; not on photographs. That is where the work is.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 style="margin-top:0">Asset types</h2>
          <ul class="clean">
            <li>Retail and neighborhood strip centers</li>
            <li>Office and flex space</li>
            <li>Small industrial and warehouse</li>
            <li>Multifamily</li>
            <li>Land and development sites</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Services</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Tenant representation</h3>
        <p style="margin:0">
          Site selection, market rent comparison, and lease negotiation for
          business owners. The landlord's form lease is a starting position,
          not a fixed document.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Landlord representation</h3>
        <p style="margin:0">
          Marketing vacant space, qualifying prospective tenants, and structuring
          terms that hold their value over the life of the lease.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Acquisition</h3>
        <p style="margin:0">
          Sourcing, underwriting, and due diligence coordination for investors
          buying income property in Collin County.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Disposition</h3>
        <p style="margin:0">
          Positioning and marketing an asset to the buyer pool most likely to
          pay for it, with financials organized before it goes to market.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap section">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Commercial property management</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        I also manage commercial property, which means the same person who
        understands the lease is the one enforcing it. Details and fees are on
        the owner services page.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/owners">Owner services &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band-jade">
    <div class="wrap section">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Request a market analysis</h2>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)">
        Tell me the asset and the goal &mdash; acquisition, disposition, or a
        lease decision &mdash; and I will put together the numbers.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:1.75rem">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Start a conversation</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+19728157644">Call 972-815-7644</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
